comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T12:04:50.236Z","harness:claude-code",CodeRabbit review on PR #1734 pointed out that flipping PM_LOCAL_RUNNER does not retarget a job that has already selected pm-local-pmcli; GitHub can leave such a job queued for 24 hours. Added an acceptance criterion for a bounded cancellation and re-run of those queued jobs on hosted runners.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T09:56:49.317Z","harness:claude-code","Local runner capacity, 2026-11-15, relayed by the fleet's Raspberry Pi CI session:\n- **Usable:** three Pi 4B hosts can run CI; one of them was restored that morning on a new power supply.\n- **Light work only:** one Pi 3B+.\n- **Out of service:** one Pi 3B+, until its power supply is replaced.\n- **Runner controller:** owned by the fleet session pm-cli-02. It places at most one ephemeral runner (3 CPUs / 2.5 GB) per Pi 4B. Routing pm-cli onto it means asking that session to add pm-cli to its repos configuration (arm64 pool); never register runners by hand or start a second controller.\n- **Cost caveat for this item:** the WAN is slow (about 85 KB/s), so routed jobs should skip setup-node's npm cache. `~/.npm` and the Node 22/26 toolcache are already persistent volumes there, and setup-bun should be pinned.\n\nThis is arm64 capacity. The x86 omarchy runner this item proposes stays the primary design, and the Pi pool would be an additional, arm64-only lane."
body: ""
